<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4440"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 7:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Great additions, Mike, thanks.  I don&#39;t recall <BR>you stating what ethnicity you believe BTK to <BR>be.  White or hispanic?  BTW, I absolutely <BR>agree with you on the age of BTK - that is one <BR>item I felt he was lying about {being born in <BR>1939.&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4440-->
<!--Post: 4441--><!--Time: 1106364172-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4441"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 7:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t have any strong indication on ethnicity with what I have in hand. This kind of thing is ironically pretty tough without reference to a case file. I know it sounds like it should be an easy first step but it isn&#39;t. There have been some REAL blunders made by profilers on just this point.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4441-->
<!--Post: 4445--><!--Time: 1106366490-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4445"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 8:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My first serious mistake has been made, as your profile indicates he wasn&#39;t sexually dysfunctional. Have you any thoughts why he didn&#39;t rape any of his murder victims? Finally, given this sexuality, do you lean more toward probable or improbable as to BTK having been a serial rapist before blooming into a murderer?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4445-->
<!--Post: 4452--><!--Time: 1106369967-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4452"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 8:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, what importance did religion play, do you think, in his life? Do you feel that he might have had some kind of long-term church affiliation? I do not think he himself actually has any faith - that would be decidedly non-sociopathic, to have a sincere religious faith - but church would have facilitated contact with others and enabled him to preserve a definite veneer of normalcy.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4452-->
<!--Post: 4455--><!--Time: 1106374602-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4455"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 10:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George: <BR> <BR>I wouldn&#39;t say that you&#39;re wrong. It seems to me that he has a psycho-sexual dysfunction, or worse. He is clearly not a rapist/killer type, but that doesn&#39;t mean he is sexually functional and normal. I would very much doubt that he was a serial rapist at any point. In fact, it seems to me that his behavior was/is driven by fantasies that he cannot bring to complete fruition. Remember that many kinds of relationships, normal and otherwise, are based on drives other than sex -- control, for example.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4455-->
<!--Post: 4456--><!--Time: 1106374899-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4456"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 10:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve: <BR> <BR>That&#39;s a bit of a hard one to answer, given what little I know. I suspect that he might have been exposed to religion through his mother in his formative years. He may have had it jammed down his throat by his father &#40;pure guesswork&#41;. However, I agree with you that he probably has no real religious convictions, even if he has an affiliation. He may use religion to his advantage in relationships or as a control mechanism but I have a hard time accepting that he has any REAL belief system at all.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4456-->
<!--Post: 4468--><!--Time: 1106394667-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4468"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 3:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hello Mike,  <BR>Do you suspect BTK of being a constant liar. Habitual. Ive read this is often the case.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4468-->
<!--Post: 4471--><!--Time: 1106399526-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4471"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 5:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mr. Kelleher, thank you. There may be thousands of married couples who simply don&#39;t engage in sex. <BR>Quite true. <BR> <BR>That reminds me of someone who said, in the jaded 1980s, that life boiled down to two things: <BR>&#34;Money and Sex, in that order.&#34; Money, of course, is power, and power can easily be used to control. <BR> <BR>One other, as it&#39;s funny. The &#34;Simpsons&#34; cartoon show. Evil Montgomery Burns, local billionaire, says to his toady, &#34;Oh, what&#39;s the point of having money if you can&#39;t intimidate people with it!&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4471-->
<!--Post: 4490--><!--Time: 1106420380-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4490"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 10:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nugzter: <BR> <BR>Yes. He is an accomplished liar and manipulator. It is habitual and prevasive. He will tell the truth only when it serves his need to further another lie or exercise control over a person or situation. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4490-->
<!--Post: 4524--><!--Time: 1106477421-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4524"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 2:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks for the speedy answer Mike. I got another one for you. My girlfriend opened my eyes to this theaory.  <BR>Do you think its possible that BTK is not a sexualy driven SK, but instead a revenge driven SK, and that he is desguising his motives to throw the police and profilers off track? We arlready know he is a liar.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4524-->
<!--Post: 4543--><!--Time: 1106514239-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4543"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 1:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nugzter: <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t think that&#39;s likely. It&#39;s possible that the Otero attack had an element of revenge but I don&#39;t think that BTK&#39;s signature is based on that. Rather, I tend to think of him as a sexual predator who thrives on control over the sexual aspect itself. In other words, the sexual component is very much secondary to the need to dominate and control his victims - it may even be sublimated. This is not an uncommon type of killer. However, it differs from a serial rapist that was discussed earlier in the thread. This has led me to wonder about some kind of victim connection that has not yet been discovered or made public. The case files would tell us more, I&#39;m sure, but they are not likely to be available anytime in the near future. Perhaps some very sharp researcher close to the scene can find some connection between/among victims. It may seem tenuous but I think it would be a worthwhile effort. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4543-->
<!--Post: 4544--><!--Time: 1106514590-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4544"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 1:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Let me just add one other thought. His first kill will be the most revealing. It will likely be a &#34;comfortable kill,&#34; by which I mean he probably had some connection with the victims, knew or lived in the nearby area, and understood that he would be safe if he killed according to his original plan. That kind of thing requires lots of fantasy and a good deal of planning. So, the motive for the first attack is more direct than the later attacks, probably. However, he found that he liked killing, he liked the domination and sense of release/relief that came with it, and he liked the empowerment most of all. In this sense, he was/is a lot like Zodiac and similar killers, who love to poop on society as much as possible since it was society who rejected them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4544-->
<!--Post: 4553--><!--Time: 1106518072-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4553"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 2:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, what kind of clues lead you to your conclusions? Profiling is an awesome tool, but i just wondered what clues led you to some of the specfic details. The movie collection, playing a stringed instrument, being a youngest child ect. Also do you have access to clues that are beyond public knowledge, police or investigators? thanks<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4553-->
<!--Post: 4555--><!--Time: 1106518743-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4555"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 2:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Profiling is an awesome tool? <BR> <BR>No disrespect, but the Beltway Sniper profile was as wrong as wrong could be, as was the Louisiana Serial Killer. <BR> <BR>To me it&#39;s all educated guesses.  I bet money if the BTK is ever identified he was in his early to mid 30s when he began killing.  He is OCD as to order and everything has it&#39;s place.  He knew each of his victims names well in advance of the murders and he had the murder planned down to the very last details.  He is a planner in his life as well.  Clutter is unacceptable. <BR> <BR>If his love of trains is true, I bet you he has several model trains that he lovingly put together and that he displays with great pride. <BR> <BR>But then that&#39;s just my thoughts, which is basically all that a profile amounts to. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4555-->
<!--Post: 4565--><!--Time: 1106532168-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4565"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 6:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jrl, when was the last time you were paid to be a profiler? Thats what i thought. Its just a tool, I never believed it alone will solve the case. BTW how much money you planning on betting?  Also, theres no way he had it planned out to the last detail. And i think OCD is not likely but possible. Again i would like mike to explain where he gets some of his profile from.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4565-->
<!--Post: 4566--><!--Time: 1106532507-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4566"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 6:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s interesting to see such opposing views right next to each other. Profiling can be very helpful or very distracting, right or wrong, informed or uninformed. Its purpose is not to solve cases but to limit the universe of potential suspects. In some hands it can be a great tool, for others it&#39;s an ego trip that won&#39;t quit. So, it&#39;s like a lot of other things in life, good and bad. When I first published my &#34;typing&#34; for female serial killers a lot of folks went nuts. Some immediately started using it in advanced and post-grad programs, others said that I was a madman &#40;or worse&#41;. Frankly, there are just too many egos in this end of the business for my liking. So, I just go about my life and let the rest of the world do the same.  <BR> <BR>Each profiler has his/her own technique and speciality. When they work, they&#39;re great. When they don&#39;t, they can be a real disaster. Either way, it all gets too much hype for my dime. <BR> <BR>End of final sermon on profiling and back to the thread &#40;sorry, Tom&#41;. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4566-->
<!--Post: 4567--><!--Time: 1106532536-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4567"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 6:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Paid to be a profiler?  I wouldn&#39;t steal from someone like that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4567-->
<!--Post: 4569--><!--Time: 1106532707-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4569"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 6:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bulldog: <BR> <BR>Sorry, I didn&#39;t mean to ignore your question. There is no way I can explain to you how I develop profiles, behavioral or criminal. It would take several books, which I don&#39;t intend to write. Perhaps the most important element is lots and lots of experience. It also helps to learn by working with really good people in the business. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4569-->
<!--Post: 4583--><!--Time: 1106551883-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4583"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 11:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, What other unsolved series of murders match up with BTK&#39;s? An example of a similar killer might be the Original Night Stalker, who killed at least 10 people in Orange County, CA, in the late 70&#39;s - early 80&#39;s. I <u>don&#39;t</u> think this was BTK advancing his methods, becoming more aggressive, but I do wonder if studying similar patterns, murders that have similar methods behind them is instructive. Have you compared, as part of your profiling process, other killers to BTK? He himself mentioned Harvey Glatman, for one. I&#39;ve wondered if that might indicate that a good knowledge of Glatman, his personality and crimes, might be instructive in figuring out BTK. <BR> <BR>BTW - of the profiles I&#39;ve read online, yours is the one that seems the most sensible to me. I&#39;m convinced.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4583-->
<!--Post: 4584--><!--Time: 1106551892-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4584"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 11:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dr. James Brussel, a criminal psychiatrist and one of the first criminal profilers was instrumental in the capture and arrest of George Metesky who was the Mad Bomber of New York in the 40&#39;s and early 50&#39;s. Brussel was at first at a loss to profile the bomber but once he was given the police case file he hit the nail on the head. <BR>Brussel profiled the bomber as indeed mad and middle aged around fifty,  a former Con Edison employee, neat and meticulous, a foreinger or someone who spent time with foreign people, probably Slavic and devout Catholic, lived in Connecticut not New York, lost his mother young, lived with an unmarried female relative, had a least a high school but no college education, was a neat conservative man and when arrested would be wearing a double breasted suit. Buttoned. <BR>The profile so infuriated the mad bomber that he personally called Brussel to tell him to stay away from the case.  <BR>The bomber turned out to be 53 years old, very neat and meticulous, had a high school education but no college, was a  steady church attending Catholic, was Slavic, lived in Waterbury Connecticut with his two unmarried sisters, had lost his mother at a young age and was a former Con Edison employee. He was wearing a bathrobe when police came to his door and he confessed. They alowed him to change into clothes and he put on a neat conservative double breated suit which he buttoned up all the way. He was found insane. <BR>I would like to see Mr. Kelleher have access to the BTK case file. Is there any chance this could happen?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4584-->
<!--Post: 4600--><!--Time: 1106574997-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4600"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 5:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve: <BR> <BR>Yes, I&#39;ve looked at comparisons and nothing really jumps out at me as a copycat issue or even a pattern issue. However, he is familiar with other serial killers and wants to claim his position among them. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4600-->
<!--Post: 4602--><!--Time: 1106581160-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4602"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 7:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, <BR> <BR>Thank you, thank you for the additions to your profile.  You hit on several key items that I felt strongly about. I, too, wish you had access to the case file and if WPD and the other &#39;experts&#39; on the case &#40;FBI, etc&#41; would allow that, they might realize that solving this case might come from just one small clue they&#39;ve overlooked. <BR> <BR>In your original profile, you said you believed he had a college degree.  His letters, however, seem to indicate a very poor grasp of literacy - very strange for someone who fancies himself a poet.  Do you think his letters are deliberately poorly written?  I haven&#39;t spent a lot of time really digging for the inconsistencies you would expect to find if that was the case. <BR> <BR>And secondly, I believe that BTK either didn&#39;t have a car or didn&#39;t use it, and relied on public transportation.  It would make sense that he didn&#39;t own one in 1974 when the Otero&#39;s were killed, especially in light of the gas crisis in 1973.  Reviewing the locations of the victims, main streets, plotting the area into grids, and overlaying the Wichita transit maps, you can get a feeling of how easy that might have been for him - especially in the Fox killing and subsequent phone call.  The part I haven&#39;t been able to fully research is how the schedules and stops may have changed over 30 years. Do you have a feel for this? Could he have been accessing public transportation and if so, was it such a regular method of transporation that he would never be noticed?  We hardly notice the familiar faces of strangers we see everyday.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4602-->
<!--Post: 4612--><!--Time: 1106587634-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4612"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Murco<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Murco<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 9:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->mike, <BR>don&#39;t you think btk would be very interested in the Abu Ghraib prison abuse scandal? and perhaps was very &#34;excited&#34; by the photo&#39;s that were circulated on the web. i know he resumed communicating in march &#39;04, and the prison scandal didn&#39;t erupt until the end of april &#39;04, but i figure this probably added fuel to his re-emergence. i think it is probable that someone close to him may have noticed him going &#34;overboard&#34; with the whole Abu Ghraib thing, and/or made a mental note of strange comments he has made re: abu?     <BR>what kind of effect do you think a thing like the iraq prison abuse scandal &#40;media blitz&#41; would have on a sexual sadist like btk? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4612-->
<!--Post: 4613--><!--Time: 1106587712-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4613"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 9:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, my original profile still stands. It seems that Tom replaced the original with my additions, which was not my intent. I guess we got our wires crossed. Anyway, in my view, the mistakes in the letters are faked. There are just too many complex components in the letters that he got right to make the simple and obvious mistakes that appeared. It was/is a red herring, just like Zodiac used to write. And, no, I don&#39;t believe they were the same person. <BR> <BR>The car issue is an interesting one. I really have no strong opinion about this. Some facts lead one way, some the other. The most logical conclusion is that he had a car but didn&#39;t use it actively in his crimes. That&#39;s pure guesswork on my part. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4613-->
<!--Post: 4615--><!--Time: 1106588578-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4615"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 9:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike_Kelleher <BR> <BR>In another post, it&#39;s stated that BTK used the ice trays because he liked the thought of the &#34;shocking&#34; feeling the victims would get when he put his cold hands on the victims throats.  <BR> <BR>Do you think it maybe remotely possible that it is not that at all but maybe a type of tactile/sensory defensiveness? Maybe he has a &#34;thing&#34; about the way things &#34;feel&#34;. People who suffer from this disorder as adults have many other problems one of wich would explain the way he spoke on the phone in the 911 tape. People who have this dysfunction often have speech and language delays.  <BR> <BR>It&#39;s just a thought, it would help to explain the semen although I know that quite a number of serial killers do this. But it may explain the semen and no sexual assault. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4615-->
<!--Post: 4626--><!--Time: 1106599027-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4626"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 12:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mr. Kelleher, <BR> <BR>In your higher probability of BTK&#39;s birth year you write 1949-1951. Have you noticed anything unusual which would lead to this small brackett?  <BR> <BR>Traditional profilers underscore the difficulty regarding the age aspect of profiling - often using Shawcross as one example. Or, is the birth year difficulty not quite as tough as asserted, but more a preemptive CYA for yet another crumbling shibboleth promulgated by early profilers who obtained their information in the 1970s and have altered it very little?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4626-->
<!--Post: 4643--><!--Time: 1106617111-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4643"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 5:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Topsailgirl: That&#39;s a bit too speculative for me. <BR> <BR>George: Well, I&#39;m not a very traditional profiler &#40;just ask any profiler&#41;. Yes, there are a number of things that lead me to that rather narrow time frame. In general, it&#39;s based upon his use of language and experiences &#40;both what we know and what he claims/lies about&#41;. If I&#39;m off, I&#39;d hope it would not be by much, but you never know. I found his birth year claim of 1939 to be interesting, though, and that played a part in my decision. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4643-->
<!--Post: 4655--><!--Time: 1106627530-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4655"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 8:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike- <BR>I respect your work on this case very much, however, I guess I just can&#39;t get attached to the &#39;49-&#39;51 born date. <BR>That would mean that B..  could have been 23-25 years old.  I guess I just don&#39;t view someone with that little of life experience to be able to be cunning enough to keep out of jail.  I just think all the games are too advanced for a young adult of that age. <BR>But I don&#39;t necessarily agree with &#39;39 either.  I agree it&#39;s probably misinformation...I just don&#39;t know about &#39;49-51. <BR>You&#39;re the expert!  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4655-->
<!--Post: 4656--><!--Time: 1106628263-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4656"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 8:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, Wade, you could just as well be right. Hopefully, we&#39;ll all find out some day. I would much rather be completely wrong and have BTK off the streets than completely right and have him running around loose out there.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4656-->
<!--Post: 4672--><!--Time: 1106664221-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4672"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 6:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Wade/Mike, <BR>IMO, BTK is of a high enough intellect, that even in his early years, the monster &#34;play the game to his liking&#34;, and outwitted the small town police at the time, and with age/experience even now.  I totally agree with you Mike on your thoughts concerning his writing incomptetance.  I too believe that he is purposely misleading everyone with the way he appears to communicate in writing.  I also happen to have a POI that is born in 1949, and it seems much more likely that this is BTK&#39;s birth era.  Only time will tell...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4672-->
<!--Post: 4673--><!--Time: 1106664993-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4673"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 6:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, <BR> <BR>Enjoy your perspective, thanks for participating...many people assume BTK had to be in jail or moved away because there is no way he can control himself...what are your thoughts on this?   <BR> <BR>Stealth<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4673-->
<!--Post: 4678--><!--Time: 1106666936-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4678"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Birdieict<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Birdieict<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 7:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Regarding the 23-25 year old range, in the 70&#39;s, young adults were much more mature than they are now. I believe whatever power contols BTK&#39;s actions during the crimes evaporates when his emotions are under contol again. He could&#39;ve eluded being caught when in its grip, but have  been very immature as he went about daily life.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4678-->
<!--Post: 4713--><!--Time: 1106691230-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4713"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 2:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you, Mr. Kelleher, <BR>That you&#39;re not a traditional profiler - my definition of which is one who was probably with the FBI and has probably written more than one book since retiring - is exactly why I enjoy your perspective. Not to diminish anyone&#39;s pioneering work, but really, times do change and there seems to be a reluctance for many profilers to acknowledge this. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4713-->
<!--Post: 4792--><!--Time: 1106753669-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4792"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 7:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Mike, <BR>       What,if anything do you make of the detail about Joe in the Otero letter? That is,that he had a rib injury from a wreck a few weeks before. <BR>Do you think this was information uncovered during the course of the crime?  <BR>I imagine that it&#39;s something that might come out,as he was tying them up perhaps. Other than that, do you feel he would engage in conversation outside of what was necessary? <BR> <BR>Also, a curious statement from the same letter was that the next victim was already selected, but he didn&#39;t know who that was. <BR>Do you believe there could be some underlying pattern to his selection? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4792-->
<!--Post: 4836--><!--Time: 1106769027-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4836"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 11:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There is probably a pattern to his attacks but we don&#39;t have enough public information to make heads or tails of it. There may be some interesting material in the case files on this point. The rest is up for speculation, for now. Every time he leaves a communication he also leaves a bit of a trail. If WPD has some sharp folks working the case, they already know this and are trying to put the puzzle together from his recent communications.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4836-->
<!--Post: 5253--><!--Time: 1106979998-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5253"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 10:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I concur with the additions to the psychological portrait of the BTK Strangler. The age of the unknown subject, his relationship with his parents, his level of intelligence, perception of women and interests seem highly plausible. A strong superego has allowed the BTK Strangler to appear respectable in public. The unknown subject would have difficulty restraining the id in sexual relations with his wife and former girlfriends.     <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5253-->
<!--Post: 5308--><!--Time: 1107042461-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5308"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 3:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, <BR>I agree with BTK being a loner. I do not think he would have any real friends. Only the people that work with him.. They would not really know him and consider him not very bright. Do you still believe he would have been married or be married. I think he would have a hard time having any long term relationship with a woman. Because of this I think the police will have a hard time with any worth while tips. As the people who really know this man would be either dead like his parents or estranged like any siblings. These would be the only people who might be able to point the police in the right direction because they would be the only person would really know what btk is like. Their best bet to catch him I believe is the new communications as you have stated. If someone sees him dropping one off. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5308-->
<!--Post: 5315--><!--Time: 1107046502-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5315"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 4:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Scbenson&#62;&#62;&#62;  Who says he was &#34;married&#34; to a woman?  Much sexual perversion can stem from deep lying homosexual tendencies.  Perhaps he found a gay man that somehow made being a homosexual seem &#34;OK&#34;.  So, perhaps he didn&#39;t lose a &#34;wife&#34;, but a life partner.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5315-->
<!--Post: 5350--><!--Time: 1107060797-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5350"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 8:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->nah. I don&#39;t think so. What I believe is that btk would have no personal relationships. Of any kind. People know him only superfically.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5350-->
<!--Post: 5375--><!--Time: 1107075611-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5375"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 1:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To be honest, I&#39;ve flip-flopped on this issue a few times. My current sense is that he had a long-term relationship with a woman -- a relationship that kept his homicidal tendencies quiet for an extended period of time. However, your mileage may vary. I&#39;m not positive about it, just leaning in that direction.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5375-->
<!--Post: 5377--><!--Time: 1107077869-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5377"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsbarn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsbarn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 1:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok, thought I had posted this, Mike, but can&#39;t seem to find it. <BR> <BR>Here I go again. It is hard to know to a novice like myself what might be important to the investigation and what might seem like a bunch of amateur hogwosh.  I certainly do not like the idea of hanging the innocent, even if it is just in the media. <BR> <BR>As many of the posters on this board, I have located what I see as red flag. I have not read anyone else rousing suspicion of this individual, so I perhaps am being a dolt. <BR> <BR>I have found an online suspect. This person graduated from high school in Wichita in 1966 and received a bachelor&#39;s from WSU. He writes poetry and conducts business online. He writes poetry that has references to breaking into a woman&#39;s house when she is not there and what seems to be mathematically described bondage. He has also entered a contest, a la Shirley Locks, where the goal is to transform poetry of an established poet. He has lived near the crime scenes and moved from Wichita around the time of the Wegerle murder. He resembles one of the sketches and the baby photo. Now it is possible there are a cajillion people who have as suspicious a profile. What I hate to do is waste anyone&#39;s time with such an important issue as this. When the LE is gathering clues, do they ever look at something as vague as this?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5377-->
<!--Post: 5398--><!--Time: 1107106950-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5398"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 9:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Despite what some folks believe &#40;and even tout&#41;, profiling is useless for identifying a specific suspect. Its only valid use, in my opinion, is to narrow the field of suspects and, after the individual is in custody, to help in bringing out the truth in a forensic setting. Profilers who tell you that they have &#34;solved&#34; cases are not telling the truth. Profilers who tell you that a specific individual is DEFINITELY guilty should find something else to do with their lives. This is why we have a justice system. Anyway, all of this is to say that profilers are often off-base and many are just wrapped up in their own egos. It&#39;s a tool and, to that extent, it&#39;s only as good as the person using it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5398-->
<!--Post: 5407--><!--Time: 1107111179-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5407"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 10:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->ELSBARN..if you have a suspect contact the police there and tell them about what you have learned...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5407-->
<!--Post: 5409--><!--Time: 1107111404-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5409"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 10:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I could not agree with you more. Profiling has never caught anyone. In fact I believe the opposite could be argued. That it can, when improperley used hurt an investigation. I watched Datelines show on the Green River Investigation Friday Night. One thing that several detectives said was that Ridgeway was not suspected even though his name kept popping up in the investigation because he did not fit the profile. <BR>Meanwhile they concentrated on innocent suspects&#40;a cab driver for one&#41;because he did. Lessons I hope wichita police have learned from. The thing I loved about your profiling of Zodiac was it didnt fit with the portait that greysmith and others had been painting him as a mad genius. I had always thought of him exactly as your profile did. Hopefully one day your profile will be proven right. Just watch that ego when it is.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5409-->
</table></td></tr></table>
